Re-run my earlier-round API probes against this candidate:
- r13-delta-api: D-073 commit-time authorisation, evidence and sign-in;
- r12, r11 and r10 delta probes;
- regress-d066 to d069: text handling.

Verify F-DG2-480 in EN and AR.
- r13-session-end-ui, unchanged from round 13: sign-out by API, then an in-app link; plus a reload control.
- New r14-session-end-ui, five triggers while the app is open:
  - a real second tab clicks Sign out;
  - an administrator revokes the role assignment;
  - idle expiry and absolute expiry (the session row's expiry set into the past with psql);
  - logout by API.
- For each trigger the user then clicks an in-app link. Sampled for 10 s:
  - path, sign-in form, localized message;
  - stale shell (user box or sign-out button);
  - /me count, 429s and navigations to /login.
- Then a second browser context from the same IP signs in, and the same page signs in again and must land on returnTo.

checks_run.actual:
Final run: r13-session-end-ui 4/4, r14-session-end-ui 31/31, exit 0. For every trigger in EN and AR:
- one navigation to /login with returnTo=/transformations and error=session_expired;
- the form and the localized message, dir ltr/rtl, no EN leak in AR;
- /me requests in 10 s = 1, 429s = 0, no stale shell at any sample, settled in about 300 ms;
- dev.auditor signs in from a second context;
- signing in again lands on /transformations.
The reload controls make 2 /me requests. The round-13 run of this probe had looped at about 130 /me per second.
Non-zero attempts, all my probe's mistakes:
- stack-run-4-attempt1 / r14-session-end-ui-attempt1 (exit 1). The revocation case clicked My work, whose data was cached since sign-in. No request was made, so the tab could not learn the session had ended (/me=0, stayed on /my-work). The probe then crashed waiting for the input. Fixed: every trigger clicks Transformations, which is not yet loaded.
- stack-run-4-attempt2 / r14-session-end-ui-attempt2 (exit 1; 29 PASS and 2 FAIL, both in ar.revocation). The EN expiry steps had expired the probe's own API session, so the AR revocation setup failed (revoke=400). Fixed: the probe signs its API user in afresh first.
In both attempts the r13 probe itself passed 4/4.

